        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "exec is the expensive one — a fork every period",
            "Period 5s across 1000 Pods is real CPU burned",
            "httpGet comes from the kubelet, not via the Service",
            "It does not follow redirects; host defaults to Pod IP"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Timing Fields"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Field",
            "Default"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "initialDelaySeconds",
              "0"
            ],
            [
              "periodSeconds",
              "10"
            ],
            [
              "timeoutSeconds",
              "1"
            ],
            [
              "successThreshold",
              "1"
            ],
            [
              "failureThreshold",
              "3"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "successThreshold must be 1 for liveness and startup",
            "First restart ≈ initialDelay + period × failureThreshold",
            "Compute it, do not guess",
            "Startup budget = failureThreshold × period",
            "30 × 10s = 5 min grace, then it kills the container"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "startupProbe:   # replaces a fat initialDelay",
            "  httpGet: {path: /healthz, port: 8080}",
            "  failureThreshold: 30",
            "  periodSeconds: 10"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Probe endpoints: unauthenticated, cheap, own port",
            "A path behind auth returns 401 = permanent failure",
            "Readiness matters at shutdown too",
            "Failing readiness is how a Pod drains before SIGTERM"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
